# Vite emits content-hashed filenames under /assets, so they can never go
# stale — cache them until the heat death of the universe.
/assets/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

# The page itself needs no rule. It is the one unhashed file, and Pages
# already serves it at / with max-age=0, must-revalidate -- a rule for
# /index.html never matched, because Pages redirects that path to /.

# The last two are cross-origin isolation, which is what lets the page share
# memory with the audio thread and the bounce workers: decoded samples held
# once rather than copied to each, and the meters and scopes written straight
# into memory the page reads (see src/audio/shared.ts). The dev server sets
# the same pair in vite.config.ts. require-corp also blocks any cross-origin
# subresource that does not opt in through CORP or CORS; the app loads none.
/*
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy: same-origin
  Cross-Origin-Embedder-Policy: require-corp
